<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dogana della mena delle pecore di Puglia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1447–<a href="/years/1806">1806</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dogana della mena delle pecore di <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Puglia</a> was the royal customs office founded by Alfonso V of Aragon in 1447 to regulate the seasonal migration of sheep between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abruzzo">Abruzzi</a> mountains and the plain of Apulia. Based at Foggia, it allocated winter pastures on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tavoliere-delle-puglie">Tavoliere</a> and collected fees from the shepherds, providing a major revenue of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> until its abolition in 1806.</p></div>
